,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
1,"Teda language - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teda_language,"The Teda language, also known as Tedaga, Todaga, Todga, or Tudaga is a Nilo-Saharan language spoken by the Teda, a northern subgroup of the Toubou people who inhabit southern Libya, northern Chad and eastern Niger.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
2,Nilo-Saharan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/39/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..qiUd4igQzzpr0OZ7p1U9JXx2uiCs003pCBFXnawm7Uo,"Nilo-Saharan. Subgroup of 210 languages.Tedaga tuq, a language of Chad. Satellite-Core 188.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
3,Tedaga language now supported on Amara - Amara.org,https://blog.amara.org/2020/09/14/tedaga-language-now-supported-on-amara/,"Tedaga is part of the proposed “Nilo-Saharan” language family.The Nilo-Saharan language family, to which Teda belongs, spans 17 nations in the northern half of Africa and has been contested by language specialists for decades.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
4,Nilo-Saharian languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/nilo-saharian-languages/,"Saharan languages. Zaghaw (alternative name: Beria), Kanembu, Kanuri, Dazaga, Tedaga.To appear. “Nilo-Saharan and its limits”. In Jean-Marie Hombert and Gerard Philippson (eds.), The Genetic Classification of African Languages Revisited.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
5,NILO-SAHARAN: DHOLUO & GAO SONGHAY - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A_44df1whkY,О сервисе Прессе Авторские права Связаться с нами Авторам Рекламодателям...,Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
6,Teda language,https://grokipedia.com/page/Teda_language,"The Teda language (also known as Tedaga or Tudaga; ISO 639-3: tuq), is a Saharan language of the proposed Nilo-Saharan family, spoken primarily by the Teda subgroup of the Toubou (Tebu) people in the central Sahara region.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
7,Languages — Libyan Heritage House,https://libyanheritagehouse.org/language-libya,Tebou peoples of Libya and Northern Chad: Tedaga Speakers.Tedaga is the language that belongs to the family of Nilo Saharan languages and is spoken by the Teda people of southern Libya.,Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
8,"Full text of ""enwiki-Teda_language-20200725.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/enwiki-Teda_language-20200725.pdf/enwiki-Teda_language-20200725_djvu.txt,"The Teda language, also known as Tedaga, is a Nilo-Saharan language spoken by the Teda, a northern subgroup of the Toubou people that inhabits southern Libya, northern Chad and eastern Niger .",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
9,"Teda | Teda People, African Tribe & Cameroon | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Teda,"Their language, also called Teda (or Tedaga), is closely related to the Kanuri and Zaghawa languages, and it belongs to the Saharan group of the Nilo-Saharan language family. Teda has northern and southern groups; the term.",Tedaga,Nilo-Saharan
